why we need this  project 

*************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
Take a simple example.

v = 0.5 m/s

You give: 
Encoder = 0.48 m/s
IMU      = 0.47 m/s
Current  = normal

Everything is in order.
But suddenly:


Command  = 0.5 m/s
Encoder  = 0.49 m/s
IMU      = 0.20 m/s
Current  = high
LiDAR    = translation ≈ 0.21 m/s

There is a strong possibility that:

encoder motion ≠ actual body motion

This could be a wheel slip.

Meanwhile:
Command  = 0.5
Encoder  = 0
IMU      = 0
Current  = very high

Current = very high

The situation is different:

Motor stall / mechanical problem

As for:



Command  = 0.5
Encoder  = 0
IMU      = normal motion
Current  = normal


It could be:

Encoder failure

Therefore:

The sensor alone is not enough.

This is where the concept of Cross-Layer Physical Consistency comes in.
